\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Left: Temperature Scope reveals different strategies employed by LLaMA-3.2 during time-series forecasting: (a) when continuing the dynamics of a partially observed Lorenz system, LLaMA attends to regions in the input history that exhibit patterns similar to those near the cutoff. (b) When extrapolating unstructured Brownian motion, LLaMA shows diminished influence of early context. Right: Predicted probability distribution over the top 30 most probable tokens.}}{6}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lorenz brownian}{{4}{6}{Left: Temperature Scope reveals different strategies employed by LLaMA-3.2 during time-series forecasting: (a) when continuing the dynamics of a partially observed Lorenz system, LLaMA attends to regions in the input history that exhibit patterns similar to those near the cutoff. (b) When extrapolating unstructured Brownian motion, LLaMA shows diminished influence of early context. Right: Predicted probability distribution over the top 30 most probable tokens}{figure.4}{}}
